# Rows of parsed data are laid into objects by a constructor function, made by an arrow that is handed to map. The only layout of the program with the names that the constructor reads off its parameter is
# the one that this very code lays, so in the copy of the constructor the parameter was expected to be a Plate: a test that failed at every row, and the copy left for the slow version, where every store goes
# by the stub for any field. The callers of a function that instances name as their constructor are not all known; no Plate was seen to arrive: nothing is expected of the parameter.
